    "body": "## Independent exact-head review - PR444 participant read hardening blocked by private API CI\n\n**HEAD:** `f8d8a3f8e89625745bad682f0659971a0b2c8fb2`, single parent `a7314d5eac46fda46af63f10b3a82888612dd3ff`; PR444 remains OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, base PR443 unchanged `c0e6ccb11d8302b1e6f7095a063d5c93f5313f98`. Parent-to-head diff is **exactly two authorized files**: `gameplay-server/src/worker.js` (+12/-3) and `gameplay-server/test/private_api_local_test.mjs` (+51/-0).\n\n**Verdict: `READ_HARDENING_CODE_DIRECTION_OK / EXACT_HEAD_INTEGRATION_BLOCKED`**. Worker now revalidates current capability tuple using `loadAuthorized()` before replay fingerprint/result disclosure and before deriving fresh-command outcomes. The existing one-statement receipt lookup and SQL write fence are retained; post-success unguarded load remains deliberately limited to already-linearized successful commit delivery. No production/hosted/security release acceptance.\n\n**Real exact-head GitHub checks:** [CAS SQL #40159511912](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40159511912) SUCCESS (50 Python tests), [Forensics #40159511982](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40159511982) SUCCESS, [Private API #40159511938](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40159511938) FAILURE. In the actual Private API job log, isolated D1 migrations 0001-0005, cryptographic checks and new authorized SQL state/receipt predicates all passed. At `private_api_local_test.mjs:607` while calling `revokedReplay`, Node fetch failed with `UND_ERR_SOCKET: other side closed` before obtaining an HTTP response. This log does NOT establish a server crash or failed authorization.\n\n**Specific root-cause hypothesis to investigate, not yet confirmed:** the last successful HTTP test log was ~03:49:27Z; the socket failure was ~03:49:50Z after numerous synchronous `spawnSync(wrangler d1 execute)` probes that block the Node harness event loop while its undici HTTP connection remains pooled and idle. A stale keep-alive socket reused by undici is plausible. Different local/CI timings could explain nondeterminism. Inspect Wrangler child `exitCode`/`signalCode` and captured child stderr/stdout at failure, local/CI Node and Wrangler versions, HTTP keep-alive reuse and blocking durations. Do not blindly retry side-effectful HTTP calls to hide uncertainty.\n\n**Test integrity issue:** the new test first sets participant A generation=2, then status=revoked and exercises `revokedReplay` HTTP. The latter only shows denial with BOTH conditions invalid, not status-only revocation. Add separate HTTP negative cases: generation increment while status remains active, then an independently fresh capability revoked at its CURRENT generation (and/or reset generation appropriately on synthetic fixture), each preserving zero side effects. SQL-only predicate copies validate SQL shape but do not deterministically exercise Worker interleaving; retain this evidence distinction.\n\n**Next:** continue SAME Codex `Chat03B2 - Atomic Participant SQL Authorization Fence` thread, existing Draft PR444 and two-file Worker/local-test write scope. Diagnose transport closure without compromising request semantics, fix the smallest verified cause, rerun exact local workerd/D1 and *new exact-head* CI; do not widen scope, merge, deploy, use hosted D1/Cloudflare or mark pass on a single green rerun without explaining failure. User-approved checkpoint/recovery policy remains mandatory. Legacy encrypted 0003 create replay lifecycle remains separate critical deployment blocker.",
